  "P0018": {"title":"Crankshaft/camshaft position correlation Bank 2 Sensor A","causes":"The crankshaft and camshaft signals no longer line up (sensor A, Bank 2): jumped or stretched timing chain/belt, worn tensioner or guides, wrong assembly timing, faulty cam or crank sensor, or damaged reluctor.","symptoms":"Possible hard starting, rough running, misfire or reduced power.","checks":"Check for related cam/crank sensor codes. Inspect sensor mounting and wiring, then verify mechanical timing (timing marks, or chain stretch data) per service information.","repair":"Correct the timing-drive fault or replace the failed sensor as confirmed. Do not continue driving if the timing has jumped; valve damage is possible on interference engines.","prevention":"Follow the manufacturer maintenance schedule and repair confirmed faults promptly.","note":"A code points to a circuit or system; it does not prove the named part has failed. Test before replacing parts. Confirm the exact definition for the vehicle with OEM service information.","type":"generic"},
