  "P0346": {"title":"Camshaft position sensor A circuit range/performance Bank 2","causes":"Signal present but not plausible or not matching related signals: loose or misaligned sensor, damaged trigger wheel, wiring noise or high resistance, or (for timing codes) a mechanical timing/stretched-chain problem.","symptoms":"Possible hard starting, rough running, stalling or reduced power.","checks":"Inspect sensor mounting and air gap, the reluctor teeth, and wiring. Compare with the related sensor's signal; scope the waveform if possible.","repair":"Repair damaged wiring or connectors, secure or re-seat the sensor with the correct air gap, and replace the sensor only after the wiring and trigger wheel check good. If timing correlation is involved, verify mechanical timing before replacing sensors. Clear the code and verify.","prevention":"Keep connectors dry and clean, repair chafed wiring early, and follow the maintenance schedule.","note":"A code points to a circuit or system; it does not prove the named part has failed. Test before replacing parts. Confirm the exact definition for the vehicle with OEM service information.","type":"generic"},
  "P0347": {"title":"Camshaft position sensor A circuit low Bank 2","causes":"Signal voltage lower than expected: signal wire shorted to ground, open supply (for Hall-effect sensors), or a faulty sensor.","symptoms":"Possible hard starting, rough running, stalling or reduced power.","checks":"Check supply voltage and ground at the sensor, then inspect the signal wire.","repair":"Repair damaged wiring or connectors, secure or re-seat the sensor with the correct air gap, and replace the sensor only after the wiring and trigger wheel check good. If timing correlation is involved, verify mechanical timing before replacing sensors. Clear the code and verify.","prevention":"Keep connectors dry and clean, repair chafed wiring early, and follow the maintenance schedule.","note":"A code points to a circuit or system; it does not prove the named part has failed. Test before replacing parts. Confirm the exact definition for the vehicle with OEM service information.","type":"generic"},
  "P0348": {"title":"Camshaft position sensor A circuit high Bank 2","causes":"Signal voltage higher than expected: signal wire shorted to voltage, open ground, or a faulty sensor.","symptoms":"Possible hard starting, rough running, stalling or reduced power.","checks":"Check sensor ground and the signal wire for a short to power.","repair":"Repair damaged wiring or connectors, secure or re-seat the sensor with the correct air gap, and replace the sensor only after the wiring and trigger wheel check good. If timing correlation is involved, verify mechanical timing before replacing sensors. Clear the code and verify.","prevention":"Keep connectors dry and clean, repair chafed wiring early, and follow the maintenance schedule.","note":"A code points to a circuit or system; it does not prove the named part has failed. Test before replacing parts. Confirm the exact definition for the vehicle with OEM service information.","type":"generic"},
  "P0349": {"title":"Camshaft position sensor A circuit intermittent Bank 2","causes":"Signal drop-outs: loose or corroded connector, chafed wiring, cracked sensor, or a sensor that fails when hot.","symptoms":"Possible hard starting, rough running, stalling or reduced power.","checks":"Wiggle-test the harness while watching the live signal. A sensor that fails only when hot may need to be tested hot.","repair":"Repair damaged wiring or connectors, secure or re-seat the sensor with the correct air gap, and replace the sensor only after the wiring and trigger wheel check good. If timing correlation is involved, verify mechanical timing before replacing sensors. Clear the code and verify.","prevention":"Keep connectors dry and clean, repair chafed wiring early, and follow the maintenance schedule.","note":"A code points to a circuit or system; it does not prove the named part has failed. Test before replacing parts. Confirm the exact definition for the vehicle with OEM service information.","type":"generic"},
  "P0351": {"title":"Ignition coil A primary/secondary circuit","causes":"Coil, wiring, connector or control circuit fault.","symptoms":"Symptoms depend on the underlying fault; possible examples include a warning light, rough running, poor economy, hesitation, hard starting or reduced power.","checks":"Inspect coil connector and wiring; test circuit and coil using service data.","prevention":"Maintain plugs and ignition components.","note":"Coil naming varies.","type":"generic","repair":"Repair the confirmed ignition, fuel or mechanical cause on the affected cylinder(s). Repair only what testing confirms (wiring, connector, leak or failed part), then clear the code and verify with a road test and live data."},
  "P0352": {"title":"Ignition coil B primary/secondary circuit","causes":"Coil, wiring, connector or control circuit fault.","symptoms":"Symptoms depend on the underlying fault; possible examples include a warning light, rough running, poor economy, hesitation, hard starting or reduced power.","checks":"Inspect coil connector and wiring; test circuit and coil using service data.","prevention":"Maintain ignition components.","note":"Coil naming varies.","type":"generic","repair":"Repair the confirmed ignition, fuel or mechanical cause on the affected cylinder(s). Repair only what testing confirms (wiring, connector, leak or failed part), then clear the code and verify with a road test and live data."},
  "P0353": {"title":"Ignition coil C primary/secondary circuit","causes":"Ignition coil C primary circuit control circuit: wiring, connector, fuse or relay supply, the component itself, or the module driver. Cylinder assignment of coil C varies; use the service manual.","symptoms":"Possible misfire, rough running or reduced power on the cylinder(s) served by that coil.","checks":"Check the fuse and relay supply, inspect the connector, and measure component resistance against specification. Command the component with a bi-directional scan tool if supported.","repair":"Repair the confirmed wiring, connector, fuse or supply fault. Clean or replace the component only if it fails bench or scan-tool testing and the circuit is good. Clear the code and verify operation.","prevention":"Keep connectors dry and clean, repair chafed wiring early, and follow the maintenance schedule.","note":"Ignition systems carry high voltage; never touch coils or leads with the engine running. A code points to a circuit or system; it does not prove the named part has failed. Test before replacing parts. Confirm the exact definition for the vehicle with OEM service information.","type":"generic"},
