  "P0461": {"title":"Fuel level sensor A circuit range/performance","causes":"Sensor signal does not agree with the expected value or with related sensors: sensor drift or contamination, a real mechanical, vacuum or pressure problem, or high resistance in the wiring. The sender is inside the fuel tank (often part of the fuel pump module); a sticking float or worn track can cause erratic readings.","symptoms":"Fuel gauge may read wrongly or erratically.","checks":"Compare the live value with the expected value for the operating condition and with related sensors (see service data). Rule out the real condition (leaks, blockage, mechanical wear) before condemning the sensor.","repair":"Repair the wiring, connector or shared reference/ground fault found by testing. Replace the sensor only after the wiring and the real condition have been ruled out. Clear the code and verify with live data.","prevention":"Keep connectors dry and clean, repair chafed wiring early, and follow the maintenance schedule.","note":"Fuel is flammable: no flames or sparks, and relieve fuel pressure using the service procedure before opening any fuel line. A code points to a circuit or system; it does not prove the named part has failed. Test before replacing parts. Confirm the exact definition for the vehicle with OEM service information.","type":"generic"},
