  "P1128": {"title":"Manufacturer-specific powertrain code","causes":"This code is not universally defined; meaning depends on manufacturer, model year, and engine.","symptoms":"Symptoms cannot be reliably predicted without the exact OEM definition.","checks":"Identify vehicle and engine, then verify the code in manufacturer service information before testing.","prevention":"Do not use a generic guess for manufacturer-specific codes.","note":"Vehicle-specific details may vary; confirm the OEM definition and service procedure before diagnosis.","type":"manufacturer","repair":"Repair only what testing confirms (wiring, connector, leak or failed part), then clear the code and verify with a road test and live data."},
