  "P2100": {"title":"Throttle actuator control motor circuit/open","causes":"Open circuit: blown fuse, open supply or control wire, poor connector contact, open coil/winding, or a failed module driver. A dirty or carboned throttle body can also affect the motor.","symptoms":"Possible reduced power, limp-home mode, high or low idle, or stalling.","checks":"Check the fuse and supply voltage, then continuity of the control wire. Measure the component resistance (an open winding reads infinite).","repair":"Repair the confirmed wiring, connector, fuse or supply fault. Clean or replace the component only if it fails bench or scan-tool testing and the circuit is good. Clear the code and verify operation.","prevention":"Keep connectors dry and clean, repair chafed wiring early, and follow the maintenance schedule.","note":"Throttle faults can cause unpredictable throttle response; avoid driving if the engine surges or the throttle sticks. A code points to a circuit or system; it does not prove the named part has failed. Test before replacing parts. Confirm the exact definition for the vehicle with OEM service information.","type":"generic"},
  "P2101": {"title":"Throttle actuator control motor circuit range/performance","causes":"Throttle motor circuit fault or sticking throttle plate, dirty throttle body, wiring resistance or a failing throttle body.","symptoms":"Reduced power or limp-home mode.","checks":"Inspect the throttle body for dirt and binding, check motor wiring, and compare commanded and actual throttle angle.","repair":"Clean or replace the throttle body and perform the relearn procedure.","prevention":"Follow the manufacturer maintenance schedule and repair confirmed faults promptly.","note":"Throttle faults can cause unpredictable throttle response; avoid driving if the engine surges or the throttle sticks. A code points to a circuit or system; it does not prove the named part has failed. Test before replacing parts. Confirm the exact definition for the vehicle with OEM service information.","type":"generic"},
