  "P3400": {"title":"Cylinder deactivation system Bank 1","causes":"Oil pressure/level, deactivation solenoid, wiring, or control-system issue on equipped engines.","symptoms":"Warning light or reduced fuel economy/performance.","checks":"Confirm engine supports cylinder deactivation; check oil and related codes, then follow OEM diagnostic procedure.","prevention":"Do not assume this system exists on every vehicle.","note":"General reference only. Verify exact definition and test procedure for the vehicle make, model, year, engine, and reporting module.","type":"generic","repair":"Repair only what testing confirms (wiring, connector, leak or failed part), then clear the code and verify with a road test and live data."},
  "P3497": {"title":"Cylinder deactivation system Bank 2","causes":"Oil pressure or level problem, deactivation solenoid fault, wiring problem, or control-system fault on engines equipped with cylinder deactivation.","symptoms":"Warning light or reduced fuel economy/performance.","checks":"Confirm the engine actually has cylinder deactivation; check the oil level and quality, read related codes, and follow the manufacturer's diagnostic procedure.","repair":"Repair the confirmed solenoid, wiring or oil-supply fault.","prevention":"Follow the manufacturer maintenance schedule and repair confirmed faults promptly.","note":"Do not assume this system exists on every vehicle. A code points to a circuit or system; it does not prove the named part has failed. Test before replacing parts. Confirm the exact definition for the vehicle with OEM service information.","type":"generic"},
  "U0001": {"title":"High-speed CAN communication bus","causes":"A fault on the CAN network: shorted or open CAN wiring, a module pulling the bus down, low battery voltage or a failed module.","symptoms":"Warning lights, dead instruments, no-start or odd behaviour from the affected module.","checks":"Check battery voltage and the module's power and ground fuses first. Inspect the network wiring and connectors. On a high-speed CAN network, with the battery disconnected, resistance across CAN-H and CAN-L at the diagnostic connector is typically about 60 ohms (verify for the vehicle). Scan all modules for related codes.","repair":"Repair the network wiring or power/ground fault. Replace and program a module only when power, ground and wiring tests are good.","prevention":"Follow the manufacturer maintenance schedule and repair confirmed faults promptly.","note":"Network (U) code definitions follow SAE J2012 for U0xxx, but the network design varies by manufacturer. A code points to a circuit or system; it does not prove the named part has failed. Test before replacing parts. Confirm the exact definition for the vehicle with OEM service information.","type":"generic"},
