  "U0151": {"title":"Lost communication with restraint control module","causes":"Communication with the airbag/restraint module is lost: module power/ground, wiring or module failure.","symptoms":"Warning lights, dead instruments, no-start or odd behaviour from the affected module.","checks":"Check battery voltage and the module's power and ground fuses first. Inspect the network wiring and connectors. On a high-speed CAN network, with the battery disconnected, resistance across CAN-H and CAN-L at the diagnostic connector is typically about 60 ohms (verify for the vehicle). Scan all modules for related codes.","repair":"Repair the network wiring or power/ground fault. Replace and program a module only when power, ground and wiring tests are good.","prevention":"Follow the manufacturer maintenance schedule and repair confirmed faults promptly.","note":"Restraint (airbag) systems can deploy unexpectedly; disconnect the battery and wait as the manufacturer specifies before working near airbag components. Network (U) code definitions follow SAE J2012 for U0xxx, but the network design varies by manufacturer. A code points to a circuit or system; it does not prove the named part has failed. Test before replacing parts. Confirm the exact definition for the vehicle with OEM service information.","type":"generic"},
